<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Food Supply Data Desk | World Food Crisis</title><meta name="description" content="A guide to indicators that distinguish market pressure, harvest risks and food insecurity."><link rel="canonical" href="https://worldfoodcrisis.pages.dev/data/"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><script is:inline src="/assets/main.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="topline"><div class="container topline-inner"><span>Independent food-system explainers</span><span>Facts before fear.</span></div></div><header class="site-header"><div class="container header-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">F<span>+</span></span><span class="brand-words"><strong>World Food Crisis</strong><small>Facts before fear.</small></span></a><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="primary-nav"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="sr-only">Open navigation</span></button><nav class="primary-nav" id="primary-nav"><a href="/#analysis">Analysis</a><a href="/data/">Data desk</a><a href="/#guides">Practical guides</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav></div></header><main id="main"><header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>Food Supply Data Desk</span></nav><h1>Food Supply Data Desk</h1><p>A guide to indicators that distinguish market pressure, harvest risks and food insecurity.</p></div></header><div class="container page-content page-content-narrow"><div class="data-hero-cards"><div class="data-callout"><span class="side-label">Food prices</span><div class="data-value">136.0</div><p>FAO Food Price Index, September 2026; up 1.5% month on month.</p><small>Released 2 October 2026</small></div><div class="data-callout"><span class="side-label">Cereal production</span><div class="data-value">2.979 bn t</div><p>FAO forecast for 2026; second-largest harvest on record.</p><small>Released 2 October 2026</small></div><div class="data-callout"><span class="side-label">Acute food insecurity</span><div class="data-value">266 million</div><p>People across 47 food-crisis countries and territories in 2025.</p><small>Global Report on Food Crises 2026</small></div></div><p class="notice"><strong>Read the units:</strong> These figures describe different things: a price index, a production forecast and acute food insecurity in assessed crisis settings.</p><h2>What each indicator can tell you</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Best use</th><th>What it cannot prove alone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FAO Food Price Index</td><td>International commodity-price direction</td><td>Local grocery inflation or food availability</td></tr><tr><td>Retail food inflation</td><td>Consumer food-basket changes in one country</td><td>A physical shortage in a specific market</td></tr><tr><td>Crop forecast</td><td>Expected harvest and revisions</td><td>Equal access or affordability</td></tr><tr><td>Stocks and stocks-to-use ratio</td><td>Aggregate inventory buffers</td><td>Whether stocks are accessible locally</td></tr><tr><td>IPC food insecurity analysis</td><td>Severity in assessed areas</td><td>Global physical production</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Latest official context</h2><p>FAO's 2 October 2026 release said the Food Price Index averaged 136.0 points in September. Its cereal brief forecast 2,979 million tonnes of global cereal production in 2026, the second-largest harvest on record, while cereal trade outlook was lowered amid Black Sea shipping constraints. A large harvest and tighter trade routes can coexist.</p><p>The 2026 Global Report on Food Crises reported 266 million people across 47 food-crisis countries and territories experienced high levels of acute food insecurity in 2025. This is not a measure of global food stocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.fao.org/newsroom/detail/fao-food-price-index-rises-in-september-amid-weather-concerns-and-transport-disruptions/en">FAO Food Price Index release, 2 October 2026</a></li><li><a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb/en/">FAO Cereal Supply and Demand Brief</a></li><li><a href="https://www.wfp.org/publications/global-report-food-crises-grfc">Global Report on Food Crises 2026</a></li></ul><p>Start with our <a href="/articles/food-prices-vs-shortages/">food prices versus shortages explainer</a> and <a href="/articles/global-cereal-outlook-2026/">2026 cereal outlook</a>.</p></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-bottom"><span>© <span data-year>2026</span> World Food Crisis</span><span>Sources over speculation.</span></div></footer></body></html>